{"name":"Ooh la La","hex":"#dcbfd5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ooh la la","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A reply implying pretentiousness; often in response to another person's use of a big word, especially a loanword that English got from French.","An exclamation of surprise, sometimes with strong sexual connotations."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ooh_la_la"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ooh La La (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ooh La La is a 2003 Indian Kannada-language romance film written, directed and produced by Hemanth Hedge, making his debut. It features Krishna Mohan, Radhika, Arya Prasad and Sonia Agarwal in the lead roles. The score and soundtrack for the film is by Suresh Devkumar. The film was a box office success."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Ooh_La_La_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ooh_La_La_(film)","wikidata":"Q96397504"},{"title":"Ooh La La (Faces song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Ooh La La\" is a 1973 song by the English rock band Faces, written by Ronnie Lane and Ronnie Wood. It is the title song of the band's last studio album, Ooh La La."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Ooh_La_La_-_Faces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ooh_La_La_(Faces_song)","wikidata":"Q7095288"},{"title":"Ooh La La (Britney Spears song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Ooh La La\" is a song recorded by American singer Britney Spears for the soundtrack of the 2013 family film The Smurfs 2. It was written and produced by Lukasz \"Dr. Luke\" Gottwald, Joshua \"Ammo\" Coleman, Henry \"Cirkut\" Walter, with additional writing from Bonnie McKee, Jacob Kasher Hindlin, Lola Blanc, and Fransisca Hall."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Britney_Spears_-_Ooh_La_La.png?utm_source=en